id: pm-35w9l2
title: "GH-830: duplicate-safe creation must require explicit bypass before persistence"
description: "pm create detects likely duplicates but persists them and exits successfully, so agent retries and concurrent submissions silently create duplicate tracker records."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",data-quality,dedupe,github-intake,multi-agent
created_at: "2026-07-30T21:41:47.014Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-30T23:31:10.323Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-30T22:53:08.930Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-30T22:53:08.930Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Default create and copy behavior refuses high-confidence likely duplicates before persistence with a structured machine-readable result; --allow-duplicate remains the explicit audited bypass; SDK, CLI, and MCP surfaces share the policy and result contract; concurrency tests prove two equivalent creates cannot both persist; advisory mode remains opt-in and documented"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make duplicate prevention atomic and safe by default for agent-driven project creation
value: Agents can retry creation without multiplying canonical work
impact: Eliminates a primary source of graph ambiguity and duplicate lifecycle cleanup
parent: pm-33cw
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Default create and copy refuse likely duplicates atomically unless the caller explicitly supplies --allow-duplicate.
actual_result: The default preset is strict and final similarity revalidation shares a required derived-index lock with persistence; concurrency commits exactly one equivalent item.
